          "final_override": {
            "status": "WITHHOLD_COMPLETE_ROW_METHOD_CLAIM",
            "reason": "Original RS074 decision explicitly compares source empiricalAs2O3 with CHEBI30621 molecular depictionAs4O6, consults definition2:3 and PubChemCID14888, rejects arsenite replacement, and only then proposes the minimal exact oxide owner. Owner evidence and history retain that representation judgment. This affirmative trace is stronger than merely observing LLM authorship. Official ChEBI primary label is diarsenic trioxide and As2O3 is a synonym; OLS search capture classifies As2O3 among related_synonyms while its exact_synonym is the tetraarsoxane structural name. Current preferred-label equality was adopted after the documented reasoning and does not itself establish a performed primary-label lookup. The identity judgment is chemically supported at the oxide-reagent scope: official definition gives As:O2:3; primary CCAP UCM weighsAs2O3 separately from NaOH-containing primary stock; PubChem captures empirical formula and As4O6 representation corroboration. The defect concerns published LexicalMatching as the recorded method, not forcing a different oxide or an arsenite ion identity.",
